+# KARETA 188.5.5.6.84.171 — design canon host-test candidate
+
+Base: `188.5.5.6.84.170` full Plesk server-hardening package. This increment changes presentation/layout contracts only and preserves DB 138, API/business logic, Android and 84.170 server hardening.
+
+## Design canon
+
+1. Added `css/next/design_contract.css` as the shared token and global layer authority. Canonical layer scale: base 0, content 1, sticky 20, shell 40, nav 50, FAB 60, overlay 80, modal 100, toast 120, debug 200.
+2. Rebuilt the active Master shell owner in `master_shell_canonical_84_143.css` around exactly three viewport contracts: phone <=767, tablet 768–1199, desktop >=1200.
+3. Removed the 84.169 two-row 3+3 phone dock. Master phone navigation is exactly six destinations in one row: Биржа / Заказы / График / Сообщество / Запчасти / Ещё. `Сегодня` remains absent.
+4. `master_surfaces.css` is the Master content geometry owner. New canonical owners contain no raw numeric `z-index` declarations.
+5. Master Exchange is normalized in its existing component owner `master_ui_exchange_schedule_flattening.css`: client-directory search/filter language, one card on phone, two substantial cards on tablet/desktop, flat cards and responsive quick-response controls. No API/state/route changes.
+6. Known shell/viewport source layers now consume semantic layer tokens. Legacy bundles remain frozen compatibility inputs until browser acceptance proves they can be retired safely.
+7. Added deterministic `tools/build_master_runtime_css.js`, `tools/test_design_canon_84_171.cjs` and `tools/audit_design_debt_84_171.cjs`.
+
+## Preserved
+
+- Database canonical/current target remains migration 138; no migration 139.
+- 84.170 trusted-proxy IP handling, atomic rate-limit files, authorization-first diagnostics, immutable versioned static caching and Plesk gzip guidance are preserved.
+- 84.168 Service Worker/community failure handling and 84.169 route cancellation/question retry/permissions remain unchanged.
+- Android/native bridge is unchanged.
+
+## Hosting acceptance boundary
+
+Local checks prove package/static contracts only. Host test must still prove PHP-FPM/nginx/MySQL behavior, exact release/provenance, cache headers, fresh Service Worker namespace, authenticated Master two-pass navigation, phone/tablet/desktop layout and absence of mixed-release assets.
